# type_param_union_return.tkr — the F1 constrained-type-param union-return fixture. It proves a
# `<T: IOrd>` generic function may return `T | null` (the `first_or_null`/`dequeue`/`heap_pop_min`
# idiom): before F1 the checker false-rejected the return type with "an interface cannot be a variant
# member yet", because a constrained type-param registers with a synthetic InterfaceBody that
# `is_interface_name` reported as a real interface. A self-contained project (its own IOrd copy, since
# teko::cmp is compiler-internal). The narrowed gate still rejects a genuine `interface | null`.

Feature: type_param_union_return — a constrained type-param `T: IOrd` may be a `T | null` union member

  Scenario: first_or_null_present_and_empty — the union return concretizes at mono to `Num | null`
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 7
